LoadSnapshot() checks the supported version and blacklist payload. The ReadString() and ReadZone() helpers in the accompanying source provide string-length, record-completeness, and basic zone-value checks. On a detected failure, it returns a negative code and clears the output arrays. These checks provide basic validation rather than checksum-based integrity verification.
This keeps the storage format separate from the zone engine. LoadSnapshot() is concerned with reading the stored data and making it available to the caller, including the persistence format and its associated validation or version handling.
LoadPersistState() then uses those records to restore the state expected by the runtime engine.
This distinction matters because loading a record is not the same thing as recreating a runtime zone. The persistence layer can recover the stored data, but the zone engine still needs an actual CZone object that can participate in lifecycle processing and future updates.
That conversion is handled by RebuildZoneFromRecord().
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Rebuild a runtime zone from its persisted state                  |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
CZone* RebuildZoneFromRecord(
const
SZonePersist &r)
  {
   CZone *z =
new
CZone((r.top + r.bottom) /
2.0
,
                        (ENUM_ZONE_TYPE)r.zone_type,
                        r.created,
                        g_cached_atr);
if
(z ==
NULL
)
return
NULL
;
   z.name        = r.name;
   z.is_user_zone= r.is_user_zone;
   z.top         = r.top;
   z.bottom      = r.bottom;
   z.price_level = (r.top + r.bottom) /
2.0
;
   z.height      = r.top - r.bottom;
   z.created          = r.created;
   z.last_touch_time  = r.last_touch_time;
   z.broken_time      = r.broken_time;
   z.status       = (ENUM_ZONE_STATUS)r.zone_status;
   z.is_broken    = r.is_broken;
   z.is_pending   = r.is_pending;
   z.consecutive_closes_outside   = r.consecutive_closes_outside;
   z.consecutive_rejection_closes = r.consecutive_rejection_closes;
   z.buy_triggered  = r.buy_triggered;
   z.sell_triggered = r.sell_triggered;
   z.time_left  = r.time_left;
// Part V real time anchors
z.time_right = r.time_right;
   z.zone_score           = r.zone_score;
   z.Current_zone_score   = r.current_zone_score;
   z.zone_tier            = r.zone_tier;
   z.initial_volume_ratio = r.initial_volume_ratio;
   z.departure_velocity   = r.departure_velocity;
   z.touch_count        = r.touch_count;
   z.bounce_count       = r.bounce_count;
   z.failure_count      = r.failure_count;
   z.max_reaction_pips  = r.max_reaction_pips;
   z.resurrection_count = r.resurrection_count;
   z.breakout_quality   = r.breakout_quality;
   z.was_drawn          =
false
;
return
z;
  }
RebuildZoneFromRecord() takes the persisted representation and reconstructs a live zone from it. The reconstructed object is not treated as a newly detected zone.
Its saved properties and lifecycle flags are restored rather than initialized as a newly detected zone. The restored collection remains subject to the startup relevance checks.
At this stage, the logical zone state has been recovered. However, the framework has one more responsibility before restoration is complete: the chart itself must agree with that restored state.
Reconciling Restored Zones with the Chart
Restoring the logical state of a zone does not automatically restore the chart object that represents it.
The framework therefore performs a reconciliation step through ReconcileChartObjects().
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Reconcile persisted zones with chart objects                     |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
ReconcileChartObjects(
void
)
  {
//--- 1. Ensure every restored zone has a chart object (recreate if missing)
for
(
int
i =
0
; i < active_zones.Total(); i++)
     {
      CZone *z = (CZone*)active_zones.At(i);
if
(z ==
NULL
)
continue
;
if
(
ObjectFind
(
0
, z.name) <
0
)
        {
if
(
ObjectCreate
(
0
, z.name,
OBJ_RECTANGLE
,
0
, (z.time_left !=
0
) ? z.time_left : z.created, z.top, (z.time_right !=
0
) ? z.time_right :
TimeCurrent
(), z.bottom))
// Part V restore stored anchors (right edge remains framework-managed)
