OnDeinit() provides the final opportunity to save any remaining dirty state before the EA instance ends. After the final save attempt, OnDeinit() deliberately removes all rectangle objects from the chart, including unrelated rectangles. Managed zones can be recreated from a usable snapshot on the next attachment; unmanaged drawings are not included in that snapshot.
The resulting lifecycle is straightforward:
OnInit() — restore and reconcile.
OnTick() — process normally and persist changes.
OnDeinit() — attempt to save remaining dirty state.
Persistence therefore extends the lifetime of the zone engine without changing the responsibilities of detection, lifecycle management, or trading.
