Conclusion
Part V completes another important layer of the zone manager by allowing its logical state to survive beyond the lifetime of a single EA instance. The framework can now save managed zones, lifecycle flags, accumulated telemetry, price-based blacklist entries, and user-zone price boundaries and stored time anchors. On restart, it restores usable snapshots, reconciles chart objects, and applies the existing startup relevance check before normal processing.
Just as importantly, persistence remains separated from detection, lifecycle management, and trading. It extends the framework without changing the responsibilities of the systems already established in the previous parts. With the zone engine now able to retain its state across sessions, the next step is to expand where that state can originate.
